# Planning slices

- Every piece of work is split into **slices**: one **Behavior** (observable
  outcome — a slide, a claim, a script's behavior when run) or one
  **Structure** change (internal reorg, no observable change, justified only
  by the **immediate next** Behavior it unlocks).
- Decompose with **slice-planning** (`.agents/skills/slice-planning/`). Order
  by outcome, not by layer; size each slice to finish in ~5 minutes including
  checks. Write the plan at `.planning/quick/NNN-slug/PLAN.md`. Execute with
  **execute-plan** (`.agents/skills/execute-plan/`).
- **Time-box:** a fix/edit attempt over 5 minutes — scrutinize the breakdown;
  over 10 minutes — stop, stash WIP, re-decompose smaller (see the skill for
  detail).
- **Jidoka** — Before starting a slice and after finishing it: stop for
  developer judgment on value/design forks, credentials, undiagnosed
  unrelated failure, or ambiguity (see **execute-plan**). Do not stop merely
  to avoid fixing a check failure caused by the current change.
- **Wrap-up (required on execute-plan):** Jidoka → post-change-refactor →
  update plan → commit. Invoking execute-plan authorizes one commit per
  closed slice. Do **not** push unless asked. This repo has no CD deploy
  gate.
- Before committing a slice, run **post-change-refactor**
  (`.agents/skills/post-change-refactor/`) on the uncommitted change: collapse
  duplication, fix naming, consolidate shotgun surgery, delete dead/redundant
  content, split code files over 250 lines. It Jidoka-stops before
  cross-subsystem edits without explicit authorization — it never commits.
- Don't deliberately leave `pnpm typecheck` or `pnpm build` broken across a
  commit.

See also: `architecture-decisions.mdc` — durable structural decisions go
through an ADR instead of an ad hoc refactor.

## Planning layout

Ad-hoc slice plans (doughnut `quick/` naming; this repo has no GSD):

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `.planning/quick/NNN-slug/PLAN.md` | Plan from **slice-planning**. `NNN` is the next free 3-digit number at write time; `slug` is kebab-case |

- Do **not** write a flat `.planning/<name>.md` or a plan beside the deck/claim
  (`NOTES.md`).
- Do **not** add GSD files (`PROJECT.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md`, `ROADMAP.md`,
  `STATE.md`, `config.json`, `.planning/phases/`) or run `/gsd-new-project`
  unless the owner asks. `execute-plan` must not write `STATE.md`.
- Product files stay capability-named — plan and slice numbers belong only
  under `.planning/`.
- **While a plan is in progress:** keep resume-useful status and brief
  learnings in that `PLAN.md`.
- **When every slice has landed:** delete the spent `NNN-slug/` directory
  (no plan diary). Include that deletion in the last slice's commit.
